0..74 Comment "// An inductive-recursive universe, after Dybjer and Setzer: the codes and"
75..152 Comment "// their decoder are one block, because a code\'s field names the decoder. The"
153..226 Comment "// dependent function code carries a domain code and, for each element of"
227..303 Comment "// that domain\'s decode, a codomain code, so its second field\'s type decodes"
304..379 Comment "// its first. The block is one admission: the codes form with the decoder\'s"
380..457 Comment "// declared type in scope, then the decoder is checked against the codes just"
458..530 Comment "// formed, and inside the decoder\'s own fixpoint a field type naming the"
531..605 Comment "// decoder reads the fixpoint\'s binder, so the decode a field holds stands"
606..681 Comment "// below the code it came from. Nothing about induction-recursion is new to"
682..757 Comment "// the kernel: the decoder is a function into the universe, and a decode is"
758..833 Comment "// the type the code it returns quotes. The codes and the decoder are named"
834..907 Comment "// apart from the closed universe\'s, whose arrow code is not dependent. A"
908..982 Comment "// universe indexed by a level takes the same admission. Each code\'s field"
983..1043 Comment "// decodes the code before it, at the level the field holds."
1045..1061 Comment "// The naturals."
